1
00:00:00,780 --> 00:00:04,881
Before the light reaches the hill, the cherries are already red.

2
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:09,371
My grandmother planted these rows in nineteen seventy-one.

3
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:15,244
At seventeen hundred metres, coffee ripens slowly. That is the whole secret.

4
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:19,781
We pick only what is red. The rest waits for another morning.

5
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:25,380
By seven, four baskets. By noon, the mill will have all of it.

6
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:30,177
Water, then skins, then the beans. The cherry gives up everything.

7
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:34,401
The beds face east, so the sun works first.

8
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:39,018
By afternoon the patio smells like bread and wet stone.

9
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:42,841
And then, one cup. This one is ours.
